hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1740","**\nNarrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated to us Ibn Abi 'Adi, from Ibn 'Awn, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah (RA), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Indeed, within the Friday [prayer] there is an hour in which, if a Muslim stands and prays, seeking from Allah any good at that time, Allah will grant it to him.\"\n\nIbn 'Awn said: And he (the Prophet ﷺ) indicated this with his hand above his head. We said: \"Is it the last hour?\" He (the Prophet ﷺ) said: \"Rather, it is the hour in which one is in a state of prayer awaiting it.\"\n\nAbu Bakr (ibn Abi Shaybah) said: This narration indicates the permissibility of supplication while standing in prayer awaiting [the next rak'ah]."
